## Reviewer points not followed

- tr-a 4. `TWD 1.57M` is a pinned product string. A Türkiye gloss in parentheses would still have to keep that byte sequence; the suggested replacement deletes it. The verb was fixed instead.
- tr-a 6, 31, 53 and tr-b 10. The awkward glued “1” is real. Deleting it fails the number checker, because the Korean source contains those digits. The rewrite keeps the digit and fixes the reading around it.
- tr-a 36 and the U+200B “pad” are not a Turkish-only defect. The counts match the Korean source. Treating them as disposable blank lines, or promoting Q16–Q20 to headings, would fail the checker.
- tr-a 47’s request to delete the difficulty row. The English source has the same row. Deleting it changes the table. The cells were softened instead.
- tr-b 25. The short blocks are the English and Korean structure. Merging them would drop `nonEmptyBlocks`.
- tr-a 1’s “garantili görünürlük”. The sentence is negated, but `/garanti/i` fails the Turkish guidance test. “Görünürlük güvencesi vaat etmez” keeps the meaning.
- tr-b 8 quotes “mahkemede sabitlenir”. The file has “mahkemece sabitlenir” (by the court). It was changed to “mahkemece belirlenir”.

